From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Darren Shepherd <darren@obot.ai>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 00:06:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] seam: promote ControlCore to an IControlCore interface (ADR
 0001)

Everything the shell consumes moves from the concrete ControlCore onto a
new IControlCore WinRT interface, so a second engine can be dropped in
beside the cascadia one. ControlCore becomes a marker class implementing
IControlCore + ICoreState; TermControl and ControlInteractivity::Core()
are typed against the interface.

Members and events live on one interface rather than splitting the 27
events onto an IControlCoreEvents: ICoreState already sets the
one-extra-interface precedent here, and a split would add a second QI and
complicate TermControl's revoker plumbing, which is written against a
single object.

Two of the six get_self escapes could not be promoted verbatim, because
they existed precisely because their signatures are not projectable:

- SearchResultRows returned std::vector<til::point_span>. Its only
  consumer draws one scrollbar pip per row, so it now returns
  IVector<Int32> of distinct rows and the duplicate filtering moved into
  the implementation.
- The QuickFix viewport check read GetRenderData()->GetViewport() with
  both bounds under one console lock. It is now a single
  IsBufferRowInViewport predicate to keep that atomicity. Deriving it
  from ICoreState::ScrollOffset + ViewHeight would NOT be equivalent:
  Terminal::_VisibleStartIndex() reports 0 in the alt buffer while
  GetViewport().Top() does not.

A seventh get_self site, TsfDataProvider::_getCore, is deliberately left
alone: it hands out WT's internal Renderer*, which libghostty has no
equivalent for. That is the TSF/IME coupling ADR 0001 already lists as
reimplemented per engine.

Deviation from the ADR: ControlInteractivity still holds the concrete
type. It makes 58 calls across 34 core methods, most of them impl-level
(AttachUiaEngine, SendMouseEvent, LeftClickOnTerminal,
SetSelectionAnchor, GetRenderData, GetFont). Interface-typing it means
promoting ~20 more members and is a Phase 5 prerequisite, not part of
the mechanical promotion this ADR describes.

